  "ingredients": [
    "1 (14 ounce) can sweetened condensed milk",
    "1.5 cups graham cracker crumbs",
    "0.5 cup white sugar",
    "3 teaspoons ground ginger",
    "1 cup butter",
    "2 bananas, sliced",
    "2 cups heavy whipping cream",
    "3 tablespoons powdered sugar",
    "chocolate shavings",
    "espresso powder"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather ingredients. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/YKji2aNbOLp-r6cIUZlQ1R_Zn_U=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12625-Banoffee-pie-ddmfs-step1-3x4-1627-7af97401a413426a96a2350fa07e43d6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12625/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix graham cracker crumbs, white sugar, ginger (if using), and melted butter together in a medium bowl. Press mixture into an ungreased 9-inch fluted tart pan with a removable bottom or 9-inch pie pie plate.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/4OSvMQLgkMAaPVuUvz-GYVAHj3s=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12625-Banoffee-pie-ddmfs-step3-3x4-1634-02b5866c5fd54dd69e714c6a6bab425f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12625/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake crust in preheated oven until set, about 12 to 15 minutes. Cool crust on a wire rack for 15 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/tuZxn7PkEtlHWQYbZtMrkb-zdBY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12625-Banoffee-pie-ddmfs-step4-3x4-1635-97953d92378b46a687f75e9a04335cd9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12625/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spread dulce de leche in the cooled crust; arrange bananas evenly on top.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/v01Lw8kSeP5WptQv0uvb8bwdLp8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12625-Banoffee-pie-ddmfs-step6-3x4-1645-dd980d0bceff45d19f4cfcd46e7c56f3.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12625/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beat heavy cream and powdered sugar in a large bowl until stiff peaks form, about 3 minutes. Spread whipped cream over bananas.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/acSr1Pi55OUraobdItyFRZHfEbA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12625-Banoffee-pie-ddmfs-step8-3x4-1648-5317a04645c34ad5b24de959b6d562b4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12625/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Refrigerate pie for at least 2 hours to overnight. Sprinkle with chocolate shavings, cocoa powder, and/or espresso powder, if desired, before serving. This recipe was tested in our test kitchen in May 2023 and updated to use canned dulce de leche. We also reduced the amount of butter in the crust. The original recipe called for 1 cup.",
